  "query_preview": "..\n(This evening through next Tuesday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Hot and dry conditions continue today\nthrough Thursday as upper ridging remains over the southwest. High\ntemperatures remain several degrees above normal with reaching\nnear records. Winds light and variable. \n\nBy Friday through Wednesday, a low pressure system to the \nnorthwestern CONUS will push southward along the western states \nthat will bring in much cooler air with potential of having highs \nbe below normal for this time of year. As the low pressure pushes\nsouth, westerly winds for Friday increase with speeds reaching up\nto 15-20 mph, gusts up to 25-30 mph. Conditions still remain on \nthe dry side as there is little to no moisture over Nevada. At the\nsame time as the low pressure pushes south, remnants from \nHurricane Rachel will push northward into southern Nevada \nbringing increase moisture which is expected to impact by\nSaturday.\n\nChances for showers begin Saturday and lasting through Wednesday,\nwith the highest chances (40-60%) expected on both Sunday and \nMonday, with Sunday seeing the greatest amounts of precipitation. \nTemperatures will see a big dip as the cold front moves over \nNevada Friday night-Saturday morning with highs in the 80s on \nFriday, and dropping into the 70s Saturday. By Sunday, \ntemperatures expected to see another dip with highs only in the \n50s across northern Nevada, 60s in central Nevada. Overnight lows \nwill also see a drop in temperatures starting in the 40s on \nFriday, and reaching to freezing temperatures in the 20s and 30s \nby Sunday lasting through Wednesday. Chances for snow return in \nthe forecast each night however snow amounts are very low and is \nexpected to remain in the mountain peaks as snow levels drop \nslowly each day staying above 8000 feet. Breezy southerly winds \nSaturday through Monday with speeds up to 20-25 mph, gusts up to \n35-45 mph with strongest winds on Saturday in central Nevada.\n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High confidence for dry and\nabove normal temperatures today and tomorrow. High confidence for\na low pressure system moving into Nevada late Friday and over the\nweekend. High confidence of gusty winds increasing Friday with\nstronger winds on Saturday. Moderate confidence in regards to \nmoisture from a Pacific tropical storm moving into Nevada over the\nweekend bringing in increasing chances for showers. High\nconfidence in regards to much cooler temperatures moving into\nnorthern and central Nevada over the weekend. Moderate confidence\nin regards to precipitation over the weekend and lasting through \nnext week. Low confidence in regards to mountain snow over the \nweekend. Changes to wind gusts in the grids to better represent\nthe increasing wind speeds Friday.",
